+# Story RC3.1: SMS Client + Twilio Lookup (Infrastructure Slice)
+
+Status: review
+
+Epic: RC3 (Reference-Checking — Messaging & Collection) · Story key: `rc3-1-sms-client-twilio-lookup-infrastructure-slice`
+Sprint: refcheck-v1 (tracker: `_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/sprint-status-refcheck-v1.yaml`)
+
+## Story
+
+As the platform,
+I want a minimal Twilio SMS client and a line-type lookup module behind config,
+so that collection messages and fraud signals have their single new dependency isolated and safely optional.
+
+## Scope (what THIS story owns — and what it does NOT)
+
+**Owns (the infrastructure slice):**
+
+1. `server/src/notification/sms_client.gleam` — a minimal Twilio REST helper: **send SMS** + **status-callback URL** wiring.
+2. `server/src/reference_checks/lookup.gleam` — Twilio **Lookup v2 line-type** query.
+3. `server/src/config.gleam` + `server/src/server.gleam` — load the four Twilio env vars into the existing `ServerConfig` mechanism.
+4. Unit tests for both new modules (pure builders + no-op path).
+
+**Does NOT own (later stories — do not build them):**
+
+- The actual **cadence/sends logic** (who gets messaged, when, T0/T+24h/…) → **rc3-5**.
+- **Message templates / copy** (invitation SMS body, STOP notice) → **rc3-2**.
+- The **`webhooks/twilio-sms` route + `X-Twilio-Signature` verification + delivery-failure handling** → **rc3-6**.
+- Wiring the line-type result into the **`fraud_signals` payload** → **rc3-7**.
+- Any DB schema change. rc3-1 is client infra only — it reads no rows and writes no rows.
+
+The deliverable is a **callable, tested, no-op-safe** client + lookup. Callers arrive in rc3-2/rc3-5/rc3-7.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — verbatim from epics, with this story's scope note)
+
+**AC1 — SMS send goes through Twilio REST with delivery-status callback, mirroring `email_client.gleam`'s shape (AD-5).**
+Given `server/src/notification/sms_client.gleam`, when an SMS is sent, then it `POST`s to the Twilio Messages resource with the Registered Alpha Sender ID "RTenantry" as `From` (NO from-number), the recipient as `To`, the message as `Body`, and a `StatusCallback` URL — mirroring `email_client.gleam`'s REST-helper structure.
+
+**AC2 — Graceful no-op without keys.**
+Without Twilio keys configured, the client no-ops with a log line (the "shortlist email skipped" precedent) — it **never crashes a caller**. Build + unit tests MUST pass without real Twilio creds.
+
+**AC3 — Lookup returns line type and no-ops without keys.**
+Given the `reference_lookup` module, when a line-type lookup runs for a phone number, then it returns the Twilio Lookup line type (`mobile` / `landline` / `voip` / `unknown`) and no-ops without keys.
+
+**AC4 — Env vars load through the existing config mechanism; secrets never committed.**
+When the server starts, Twilio env vars (account SID, auth token, sender ID `RTenantry`, status-callback base URL) load through the existing `ServerConfig` mechanism. Secrets are never committed.
+
+**AC5 — Sentry captures Twilio API failures with context.**
+Given a Twilio API failure (send or lookup), when it occurs, then Sentry captures it with context (status / error kind / endpoint tags). The no-op-without-keys path does NOT capture (it is expected, not an error).
+
+**Verify:** one test module per new module (mocked HTTP per existing patterns — i.e. pure builders + parse functions + the Disabled no-op branch, matching how `email_client_test.gleam` tests `build_send_body` without exercising `httpc`); no-op path verified without keys; `make test-server` green.
+
